<section class="panel" id="sources">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Fact-checked, not just written</p>
    <h2>Sources & Further Reading</h2>
    <div class="panel__body a11y-list">
      <div class="a11y-list__item">
        <span class="a11y-list__tag">RESEARCH</span>
        <p>The F-pattern and Z-pattern reading patterns come from eye-tracking research by the <strong>Nielsen Norman Group</strong>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="a11y-list__item">
        <span class="a11y-list__tag">STANDARDS</span>
        <p>Contrast and accessibility figures come from the <strong>W3C's Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG)</strong>. Core Web Vitals and Lighthouse are <strong>Google</strong>'s.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="a11y-list__item">
        <span class="a11y-list__tag">LAW</span>
        <p>Privacy law references are to the <strong>EU's GDPR</strong> and <strong>California's CCPA</strong>, current as of this writing, not legal advice.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="a11y-list__item">
        <span class="a11y-list__tag">TRENDS</span>
        <p>The button style history drew on design-trend writeups from <a href="https://www.onething.design/post/what-is-neo-brutalism-ui-design">onething.design</a> and <a href="https://www.cccreative.design/blogs/differences-in-ui-design-trends-neumorphism-glassmorphism-and-neubrutalism">cccreative.design</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

